\title{Distributive action}
\author{brentyorgey}
\date{2026-01-09T15:28:44Z}
\taxon{Definition}

\p{Let #{A} be a [semigroup](0033) [acting on](0035) #{S}, where #{S} is \em{also} a semigroup.  Then we say the action of #{A} on #{S} is \em{distributive} if it satisfies the distributivity law ##{a \cdot (s \diamond t) = (a \cdot s) \diamond (a \cdot t)} for all #{a \in A} and #{s,t \in S}.}
